## Interface With Other Roles

**R1 - Audio DSP**
- Provides audio format / feature requirements.

**R2 - ML/KWS**
- Provides the trained custom-keyword model.
- Provides model input shape, preprocessing details, and class labels.

**R4 - Networking & ASR**
- Receives the keyword-detected trigger from the ESP32.
- Handles subsequent audio streaming and ASR.

**R5 - Optimization / Benchmarking**
- Uses TinyML measurements for final performance evaluation.

**R6 - Integration**
- Integrates the complete edge-to-cloud pipeline.

## Important Rule

The ESP32 should perform only lightweight local keyword spotting.
Cloud transmission should begin **after** the custom keyword is detected.



## R3 Audio Preprocessing

Current reference audio configuration:

- Sample rate: 16 kHz
- Channels: Mono
- Sample format: int16 PCM
- Frame length: 30 ms (480 samples)
- Hop length: 10 ms (160 samples)
- Window: Hann

> Note: FFT, Mel bands, MFCC count, normalization and model
> input shape are not finalized yet and will be aligned with
> the final KWS training pipeline.
